From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] ext-dce: invalidate pointer facts after removing extensions

On targets whose pointers zero-extend into a wider Pmode, REG_POINTER tells
nonzero_bits and simplify-rtx that the upper bits are zero. Removing an
extension can invalidate this fact. Copy propagation is not the whole
closure: a Pmode pointer computed by adding an offset to an affected value
can also acquire nonzero upper bits. Clearing only changed pseudos and their
copies leaves that derived pointer marked and lets combine remove a required
zero-extension.

When an extension changed, clear REG_POINTER on every Pmode pseudo of the
function before combine. This deliberately loses pointer hints for unrelated
pseudos in that function; code-size/performance validation must measure the
cost. Functions with no changed extension, hard registers and LP64 are
unaffected. The existing SUBREG_PROMOTED copy-closure reset is unchanged.

Replaces the ILP32 default-off workaround 0072 while retaining the normal
optimization defaults and explicit controls. The dump lists the cleared
pseudos; dump-on/off equivalence is checked separately.

--- a/gcc/ext-dce.cc
+++ b/gcc/ext-dce.cc
@@ -1204,6 +1204,38 @@
      closure of the original CHANGED_PSEUDOS and registers they're
      connected to via copies.  So expand the set.  */
   expand_changed_pseudos ();
+
+#if defined (POINTERS_EXTEND_UNSIGNED)
+  /* Removing an extension can invalidate the known upper bits implied by
+     REG_POINTER, including those of arithmetic-derived pointers.  The copy
+     closure above is not sufficient for those derived values.  If anything
+     changed, conservatively discard this fact for all Pmode pseudos before
+     combine can use it.  Hard registers and equal-width pointer modes are
+     unaffected.  The normal extension-elimination optimization stays on.  */
+  if (POINTERS_EXTEND_UNSIGNED > 0
+      && known_gt (GET_MODE_PRECISION (Pmode), GET_MODE_PRECISION (ptr_mode))
+      && !bitmap_empty_p (changed_pseudos))
+    {
+      bool listed = false;
+      for (unsigned int i = FIRST_PSEUDO_REGISTER; i < max_reg_num (); ++i)
+	{
+	  rtx reg = regno_reg_rtx[i];
+	  if (reg && REG_P (reg) && GET_MODE (reg) == Pmode && REG_POINTER (reg))
+	    {
+	      REG_POINTER (reg) = 0;
+	      if (dump_file)
+	        {
+	          if (!listed)
+	            fprintf (dump_file, "ext-dce cleared REG_POINTER:");
+	          fprintf (dump_file, " r%u", i);
+	          listed = true;
+	        }
+	    }
+	}
+      if (dump_file && listed)
+	fprintf (dump_file, "\n");
+    }
+#endif
     
   /* If we removed an extension, that changed the promoted state
      of the destination of that extension.  Thus we need to go
